# SOLEUS RAISE

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Soleus Raise is an isolation exercise targeting the soleus muscle to improve ankle stiffness, lower-leg endurance and Achilles tendon resilience.

Within CAS, it is considered a foundational robustness exercise supporting efficient locomotion and repeated combat movements.

---

# Philosophy

Combat athletes spend thousands of repetitions on the balls of their feet.

The soleus is one of the most continuously active muscles during striking, footwork and defensive movement.

CAS develops soleus capacity to improve movement efficiency while reducing fatigue and injury risk.

